---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/ui/PageHead.astro';
import { marked } from 'marked';

// Keep this in sync with what the site actually does. The claims below are
// tied to concrete integrations: Cloudflare Pages (hosting), Buttondown
// (/company/newsletter + the footer form), Cal.com (/company/schedule),
// Google Fonts (BaseLayout), unpkg + jsDelivr (the REPL island), and the
// Cloudflare Analytics Engine `query_farm_extension_loads` dataset.
const lastUpdated = 'August 10, 2026';

const policyText = `## 1. Who we are

Query Farm LLC ("Query.Farm," "we," "us") operates https://query.farm and publishes the DuckDB
extensions, tools, and documentation described on it.

Query Farm LLC
4990 Sadler Pl # 4336
Glen Allen, VA 23060-6122
USA

Questions about this policy or your data: [hello@query.farm](mailto:hello@query.farm).

## 2. The short version

This is a documentation and product site. There is no account system, no advertising network, and
no cross-site tracking. We do not sell personal information. The only personal data we deliberately
collect is what you hand us: an email address if you subscribe to the newsletter, whatever you write
if you email us, and your booking details if you schedule a meeting.

## 3. What we collect

**Server and network logs.** The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare processes standard
request data — IP address, user agent, requested URL, timestamp, and approximate region — to serve
pages and to protect the site against abuse and denial-of-service traffic. We use this only for
operating and securing the site.

**Newsletter subscriptions.** If you subscribe to Dispatch, your email address is submitted to
Buttondown, our newsletter provider, which stores it along with delivery metadata such as whether a
message was opened. Every message includes an unsubscribe link, and you may unsubscribe at any time.

**Email you send us.** If you write to hello@query.farm, we receive and retain your message, your
email address, and anything else you choose to include.

**Meeting scheduling.** The scheduling page embeds Cal.com. If you book a meeting, Cal.com collects
the name, email address, and any notes you enter, and shares them with us so we can attend.

**Extension usage counts.** Query.Farm DuckDB extensions report an aggregate load event so we can
publish how widely each extension is used. These events are recorded in the Cloudflare Analytics
Engine as counts grouped by extension name and date. They are aggregate figures — they do not
identify you, your queries, your data, or your machine, and the "loads" numbers shown on extension
pages are the whole of what we derive from them.

## 4. What we do not collect

We do not run advertising or behavioural-analytics scripts, we do not build visitor profiles, we do
not use tracking cookies, and we do not sell or rent personal information to anyone.

**Your queries and data stay on your machine.** The in-browser SQL shell on extension pages runs
DuckDB entirely inside your browser via WebAssembly. The SQL you type, the data you load, and the
results you get are never transmitted to Query.Farm.

## 5. Cookies and local storage

We set no advertising or analytics cookies. The site may use your browser's local storage to
remember interface preferences, such as your light/dark theme choice in the documentation. That
information stays in your browser and is never sent to us. Third-party embeds — Cal.com in
particular — may set their own cookies under their own policies.

## 6. Third parties that receive data

Loading or using this site involves these providers:

- **Cloudflare** — hosting, CDN, DNS, and the analytics store for aggregate extension load counts
- **Google Fonts** (fonts.googleapis.com, fonts.gstatic.com) — serves the site's typefaces; Google
  receives your IP address and user agent as part of the font request
- **unpkg** and **jsDelivr** — serve the WebAssembly DuckDB engine and terminal libraries used by the
  in-browser shell; these CDNs receive your IP address when those files are fetched
- **Buttondown** — newsletter delivery
- **Cal.com** — meeting scheduling
- **GitHub** — source code repositories we link to

Each operates under its own privacy policy. We link to third-party sites throughout the
documentation; we are not responsible for their practices.

## 7. Why we may process your data

Where a lawful basis is required, we rely on: your consent (newsletter subscription); the
performance of a contract or steps taken at your request (responding to your enquiries, scheduling
meetings, providing licensed software); and our legitimate interests in operating, securing, and
improving the site and understanding aggregate demand for our extensions.

## 8. How long we keep it

Newsletter subscriptions are kept until you unsubscribe. Correspondence is kept as long as needed for
the matter it concerns and for our ordinary business records. Server logs are retained on our
providers' standard schedules, typically measured in days to a small number of months. Aggregate
extension load counts contain no personal data and are retained indefinitely.

## 9. Your rights

Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or receive a copy of
your personal data, to object to or restrict certain processing, and to withdraw consent. California
residents have the right to know what personal information is collected and to request its deletion;
we do not sell or share personal information as those terms are defined under the CCPA/CPRA, and we
will not discriminate against you for exercising any of these rights.

To exercise any of them, email [hello@query.farm](mailto:hello@query.farm). We will respond within
the period required by applicable law.

## 10. International transfers

We are based in the United States, and our providers process data in the United States and other
countries. If you contact us from outside the U.S., your information will be transferred to and
processed in the U.S.

## 11. Children

This site is intended for developers and businesses. It is not directed at children under 13, and we
do not knowingly collect personal information from them.

## 12. Security

We use HTTPS site-wide and rely on established providers for hosting and data storage. No method of
transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

## 13. Changes

We may update this policy as the site changes. The revision date at the top of the page always
reflects the current version. Material changes will be noted on this page.

## 14. Contact

Query Farm LLC · 4990 Sadler Pl # 4336, Glen Allen, VA 23060-6122, USA ·
[hello@query.farm](mailto:hello@query.farm)
`;

const policyHtml = marked(policyText, { async: false }) as string;

const summary = [
  'No accounts, no ads, no tracking cookies, no cross-site tracking.',
  'The in-browser SQL shell runs entirely in your browser — queries and data never reach us.',
  'Extension "loads" are aggregate counts per extension, not per person.',
  'We never sell personal information.'
];
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Query Farm LLC handles data on query.farm — what we collect, what we never collect, and who processes it."
>
  <PageHead
    title="Privacy Policy"
    hairband
  >
    <p class="mt-6 qf-figure text-sm text-soil-600">Last updated {lastUpdated} · Query Farm LLC</p>
  </PageHead>

  <section class="pt-12 pb-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-6">
      <p class="text-[17.5px] leading-relaxed text-soil-700">
        query.farm is a documentation and product site, and it is built to need very little from you.
        This page describes exactly what is collected when you read the docs, run a query in the
        in-browser shell, subscribe to the newsletter, or get in touch.
      </p>

      <ul class="mt-8 grid list-none gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {summary.map((line) => (
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5 rounded-lg border border-field-400/50 bg-[#fffdf7] p-3.5 text-sm">
            <span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 font-semibold text-field-700" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
            <span class="text-soil-700">{line}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <p class="mt-4 text-[13.5px] text-soil-600">
        This summary is an informal overview — the full text below governs. Questions?
        <a href="mailto:hello@query.farm" class="text-link no-underline underline-offset-2 hover:underline">hello@query.farm</a>.
        See also the <a href="/legal/terms" class="text-link no-underline underline-offset-2 hover:underline">Terms of Service</a>.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-10 border-0 border-t border-soil-300" />

      <div class="qf-legal" set:html={policyHtml} />
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style is:global>
  /* Legal prose: quieter than the editorial measure, same type system. */
  .qf-legal { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; }
  .qf-legal > * + * { margin-top: 16px; }
  .qf-legal p { color: var(--color-soil-700); }
  .qf-legal h2 {
    margin-top: 34px;
    padding-top: 18px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-soil-300);
    font-size: 21px;
  }
  .qf-legal h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; padding-top: 0; border-top: 0; }
  .qf-legal a { color: var(--color-link); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(69, 99, 47, 0.4); }
  .qf-legal a:hover { color: var(--color-link-hover); border-bottom-color: var(--color-link-hover); }
  .qf-legal ul, .qf-legal ol { padding-left: 22px; }
  .qf-legal ul { list-style: disc; }
  .qf-legal ol { list-style: decimal; }
  .qf-legal li { margin-top: 6px; color: var(--color-soil-700); }
  .qf-legal strong { color: var(--color-soil-900); font-weight: 600; }
  .qf-legal code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.86em;
    background: var(--color-soil-100);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 5px;
  }
</style>
